  "description": "Proposed roof extensions to create 2no. additional storeys (third and fourth floor). Additional storeys stepped back from boundaries to reduce impact and visibility as well as form 3no. roof terraces. Extensions to create 1no. 1 bedroom, 2 person unit and 1no. 3 bedroom, 5 person unit with associated amenity, bin stores and cycle storage. \n\nExisting stairwell to be extended up to third floor with fourth floor reached via an internal private stair. Lift shaft to remain as existing (terminating at the second floor). Existing entrance lobby on the ground floor to be extended into the commercial unit to relocate the refuse store and provide space for 3no. cycle storage spaces. Existing internal room to commercial unit to be taken into common parts use and access to commercial blocked up. 5sqm total commercial floor space lost to residential common parts/ storage.\n\nExtensions to have flat roofs with single-ply membrane finishes concealed behind zinc-clad raised parapets. The top roof will have sedum roofing. The walls will be clad in zinc, with vertical standing seams. All windows and doors to be powder-coated aluminium. \n\nAdditional window openings to flank elevation (1no. at first floor and 1no. at second floor) to provide additional natural light into flats created via Class MA change of use (separate application). Windows to match existing in size and style but be partially obscure up to min. 1.7m from finish floor.",
